; Regression (2026-09-20): an unknown identifier that is the WHOLE of a return.
; The unknown-name rule covered the OPERAND position only — as a call argument
; `NoSuchConstant` is a clean `unknown identifier` plus `function not found`,
; and as the entire value of an implicit OR explicit return it was neither
; resolved nor diagnosed: rc 0, answering the zero value of the return type for
; every input, with the CALLER silent as well, so nothing anywhere named the
; identifier. Found in packages/tscaly by writing three `AssignmentKind*`
; constants that no `define` in the package declared; every gate stayed green.
; xfail: error: unknown identifier: NoSuchConstant

function implicit_tail() returns int
    NoSuchConstant

function explicit_return(x: int) returns int
{
    if x > 0
        return NoSuchConstant
    7
}

let a implicit_tail()
let b explicit_return(1)
